<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62141" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάχεια</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾰ], ἡ</span>, obscure word read (prob.) by <i><span class="en">
			Aristarch.
		</span></i> in two passages of <i><span class="en">
			Od.
		</span></i>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆσος ἔπειτα λάχεια . . τετάνυσται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.116
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθ᾽ ἀκτή τε λάχεια καὶ ἄλσεα
					Περσεφονείης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.509
				</span></i>
			; expld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔσκαφος καὶ εὔγειος,
				παρὰ τὸ λαχαίνεσθαι, ὅ ἐστι σκάπτεσθαι πυκνῶς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1619.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1667.13
			</span></i>, Sch.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάχανον,
			λαχύφλοιος</span>: <i><span class="en">
				Zenod.
			</span></i> read <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλάχεια</span>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				197
			</span></i>.</div>
